<title>UK: CRICKET-GOOCH PULLS OUT OF ENGLAND `A' TOUR PARTY.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-GOOCH PULLS OUT OF ENGLAND `A' TOUR PARTY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Former England captain Graham Gooch has pulled out of the England `A' party for the forthcoming cricket tour of Australia because of his father's ill health.</p>
<p>The 43-year-old Essex opener was due to coach the side on their seven-week tour starting on October 23.</p>
<p>He has been replaced by Middlesex batsman Mike Gatting, another former England skipper.</p>
